+prometheus-snmp-exporter (0.31.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  freshdeb: /etc/prometheus/snmp.yml is upstream's configuration now, instead
+  of Debian's placeholder without any modules. It is generated from upstream's
+  generator.yml (in /usr/share/doc/prometheus-snmp-exporter/examples) and has
+  modules for standard MIBs (if_mib, system, ip_mib, ucd_system_stats, ...)
+  and many vendors (cisco_device, mikrotik, synology, ...), and the auths
+  public_v1 and public_v2 (community "public", public_v2 is the default):
+
+    /snmp?target=192.0.2.1&module=if_mib
+
+  An snmp.yml you changed or generated yourself is kept: dpkg asks whether to
+  replace it, and keeping it puts upstream's next to it as
+  /etc/prometheus/snmp.yml.dpkg-dist.
+
+ -- freshdeb <packages@freshdeb.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
+
